# .dockerignore — keep the Docker build context small and out of any future
# bulk `COPY . .` (info disclosure if the Dockerfile ever switches away from
# its current named COPYs). The build only COPYs four named files
# (entrypoint.sh, config.kdl, layout.kdl, demo.bashrc); everything else here
# is for other consumers (docker compose, humans), never the image.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
compose.yaml

# VCS / OS / editor cruft
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
